Mission Brief

As a Senior Launch Operations Engineer,&nbsp;you’ll&nbsp;join&nbsp;the team in Germany&nbsp;that shapes how our missions come to life.&nbsp;From the moment a campaign is conceived, you are the one aligning global launch sites, synchronizing teams and defining the operational path that&nbsp;ultimately determines&nbsp;how-and whether-the rocket leaves the ground. &nbsp;

Within the global Launch Operations team, you stand at the core of our mission: transforming complex campaigns into repeatable,&nbsp;scalable&nbsp;and&nbsp;reliable&nbsp;operations&nbsp;over multiple launch sites. Your work creates&nbsp;the&nbsp;structure that enables teams across the world to execute with confidence and precision. &nbsp;

When a campaign moves from planning to execution, you step directly into the field-joining local teams on site, leading coordination efforts&nbsp;in the company, and operations both inside and outside the control room. In these moments, you carry the responsibility of turning months of preparation into a successful launch day. &nbsp; </p&

Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.

ABOUT THE TEAM &nbsp; &nbsp;

Anduril's Imaging business line designs and builds state-of-the-art imaging systems, deployed to tackle the most significant security challenges of America and its allies. Advanced Infrared Solutions operates out of our Hudson, NH location, focused on the design and manufacturing of high-performance cooled infrared cameras and Integrated Dewar Cooler Assemblies (IDCAs) that encompass Imaging products. Advanced Infrared Solutions supplies these critical components both internally to Imaging products, and externally as a merchant supplier to the broader defense, space, and commercial industrial base. &nbsp;

ABOUT THE JOB &nbsp; &nbsp;

We are looking for a Senior Mechanical Engineer to join our rapidly growing team in Hudson, NH. In this role, y ou will lead the mechanical development and transition to production of next generation infrared opto-mechanical systems. Cooled infrared systems such as these are a critical technology across all Anduril Imaging products. Their design and fabrication relies on precision alignment, extreme cleanliness, and disciplined engineering.&nbsp;If this sounds like you, please read on! &nbsp;

WHAT YOU'LL DO &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Own hardware from concept generation to real-world use.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Develop cutting-edge infrared sensors.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Utilize first principles physics as a basis for all decisions.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Build prototypes, analyze failures, and transition successful projects into production.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Support critical hardware demonstrations with customers as needed.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Contribute to the development of new optical systems by assisting in design and implementation efforts.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Define top-level system architecture trades to develop optimal system designs.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Execute in-depth and rigorous opto-mechanical and electro-mechanical designs.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Mentoring junior engineers, leading small teams, and managing projects/budgets.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Travel to test sites as needed.&nbsp; &nbsp;

REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Bachelor's in mechanical engineering (BSME), or MS with 8 plus years of experience in design, hardware, or integrated product development and testing, and excellent leadership/communication&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Experience in an immersive interdisciplinary technical project.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Proficiency in various CAD tools and openness to using new software, with the ability to create high-quality engineering drawings that meet industry standards.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Strong skills in material selection, component sizing, system design, and troubleshooting.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Ability to navigate Change Control processes to enact changes to in-production hardware.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Understanding of thermal and structural analysis.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Exceptional analytical, troubleshooting, and root-cause analysis skills.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Demonstrated hands-on fabrication skills.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Ability to integrate electronic components into mechanical designs (motors, controllers, sensors, etc.).&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Experience with machining and fabrication processes, sheet metal, injection molding, and 3D printing.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Knowledge of industry standards (e.g., ASME Y14.5 GD&amp;T)

About MPU

More Perfect Union is an advocacy, journalism, and education organization with a mission to build power for the working class. Since launching in February 2021, More Perfect Union’s Emmy award-winning coverage has garnered 8 million followers and subscribers. We are the fastest growing news/politics YouTube channel.

About the Position

The Vertical Video Producer plays a crucial part of More Perfect Union’s journalism by driving on-the-ground coverage of active fights across the country. They will pitch, conceptualize, research, and script short, news-driven videos that mobilize viewers against corporate power and corruption while empowering the working class. The ideal person for this role is an experienced reporter with strong skills in storytelling, visual journalism, building source relationships, scripting, and pre- and post-production of vertical videos.

The Vertical Video Producer must be immersed in and excited about the process of telling stories through video and creating viral news moments with substance. They must have the technical, narrative, and relational skills to create powerful moments that hook viewers and keep them watching to the end. The position requires a high level of self-sufficiency, strong collaboration and communication skills, the ability to write clearly and meet deadlines, and a desire to engage in key policy debates and grow our audience.

Core Responsibilities

• Pitch, produce, and script short original videos (

• Pitch, research, write and host short, news-driven direct-to-camera videos for vertical video platforms.

• Identify interview subjects, write interview questions and shot lists, draft scripts, record VO or shoot direct to camera, review and provide feedback to editors on videos, including visuals throughout scripts.

• Develop and maintain relationships with sources;

• Participate in meetings and collaborate with other video team members.

• Knowledge of current social platforms and the best practices surrounding these platforms.

• Receive assignments from supervisor and colleagues for prompt action;

• Manage multiple projects simultaneously and meet expected deadlines

• Maintain high standard of work in a nimble, fast paced environment

• Perform other duties as assigned

Experience/Qualifications

• 3+ years experience in journalism/video production/social media content creation

• An excellent scriptwriter, producer, storyteller and collaborator, with strong interpersonal skills and experience in on-camera work;

• Existing source relationships with policy experts, labor leaders, advocacy organizations and other potential resources for finding leads and news stories;

• Strong editorial judgement, understanding of journalistic practices and ethics, and experience working within a fast-paced news cycle;

• The ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and meet hard deadlines;

• Proven ability to grow audiences on social media is a plus, particularly for TikTok, Instagram, and YouTube;

• Passion for, and substantial knowledge of, national politics and economic justice issues;

• Available full-time hours and able to excel in a remote/work from home environment;

• Proficiency with Adobe Premiere as well as in-platform editing tools on TikTok and Instagram a plus;

• Experience managing interns or fellows is a plus;

• Experience producing and scripting YouTube content strongly desired

